messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: example/icu.c
Line: 229
Function: main
Bug type: null-pointer-dereference
CWE: CWE-476
Explanation: If xmlCtxtReadDoc fails (e.g., unsupported encoding, ICU setup failure, or memory error), doc is NULL. xmlNodeGetContent(NULL) will return NULL, and passing this to printf with "%s" causes undefined behavior and typically dereferences a NULL pointer, leading to a crash.

Source context:
```c
      189:         ret = icuOpen(name, 0, &outputCtxt);
